      "r8_intrinsic": "Very soft low-contrast mottling with no discrete gravel, scuff edges, crust plates or cracks. Reads as fine powder/silt and remains smoother and more diffuse than cantonment or gravel at128.",
      "comparison_r7": "Clear improvement in quietness: r7 has conspicuous repeated bright cloudy perimeters and dark patches at128/64/32. r8 strongly subdues those same forms; no equally strong ridge/shadow cue remains. Mild recurrent cloud placement is still detectable when searching for it.",
      "comparison_retained_pan_r3": "r3 is smoother and almost featureless, relying strongly on tone even at128. r8 adds a restrained fine/diffuse film pattern at128 while preserving its fine-sediment character. It does not recover a unique geological identity, but that is unnecessary for a useful quiet pan treatment.",
      "distinction": "At128 it has a softer/finer structural quality than gravel and cantonment beyond lightness. Compared with the other smooth retained family members, semantic identity still depends on palette, placement and labels.",
      "repeat_and_false_read": "No obvious cracks, cells, hard seam or strong false relief. Repeated mottling is faint rather than a dominant broad diagonal/ridge landmark.",
      "distance": "At64/32 identity is primarily palette/average tone with faint mottling. This is an explicit limitation, not a rejection condition.",
      "reason": "Retain r8 pan as a visual review candidate: it meaningfully corrects r7 and adds modest128 surface information relative to r3 without a conspicuous new defect. This recommendation is not human artwork approval."
